  "facts": [
    "When the Bear Mountain Bridge opened on November 27, 1924, its 1,600‑foot main span made it the longest suspension bridge in the world, a record it held for 19 months until the Benjamin Franklin Bridge surpassed it.",
    "The 1922 charter that finally brought the bridge to life shifted its purpose from a railroad to an automobile crossing, securing a $4.5 million bond and a future transfer to New York State in 1962.",
    "In 2000, the Bear Mountain Bridge pioneered a polymer‑based, non‑toxic cable paste that eliminated the hazardous red lead paste, proving a cleaner, longer‑lasting solution for cable maintenance."
